==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|ernestly}}, from {{inh|en|ang|eornostlīċe|t=earnestly, strictly}}, equivalent to {{af|en|earnest|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɝnɪstli/|a=GenAm}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɜːnɪstli/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-earnestly.ogg|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In an [[earnest]] manner; being very sincere; putting forth genuine effort.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1900|author=L. Frank Baum|title=The Wonderful Wizard of Oz|chapter=23|passage=The Scarecrow and the Tin Woodman and the Lion now thanked the Good Witch '''earnestly''' for her kindness; and Dorothy exclaimed:}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Patrick Reilly|title=500-pound rapper suing Lyft over ride denial asks for couch over chair at ‘Breakfast Club’ interview: ‘This is accommodation’|magazine=w:New York Post|url=https://nypost.com/2025/02/11/us-news/500-lb-rapper-suing-lyft-asks-for-couch-at-breakfast-club-interview/|date=2025-02-11|passage=“This the only seat y’all got?” Demoss, who also goes by Dajua Blanding, asks '''earnestly'''.}}

